      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:640px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">Norway is not an EU member, so it sits outside the EU's GSP duty-free arrangement that applies to most other European markets on this list — Norwegian apparel imports from Bangladesh face Norway's own tariff schedule via EFTA/GSP arrangements, which we factor separately into landed cost estimates rather than assuming EU terms apply. Norwegian buyers share the broader Nordic emphasis on sustainability documentation seen in Sweden and Denmark.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Norway Trade Terms</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">EFTA Duty-Free Benefits for Norway</h2>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:600px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">As an EFTA member, Norway provides duty-free access for Bangladesh garment exports under GSP arrangement. Most apparel categories enter Norway with zero customs duty. Norway has confirmed a three-year duty-free/quota-free (DFQF) extension past Bangladesh's November 2026 LDC graduation, alongside similar extensions from the EU, UK, and Canada — so this benefit isn't at immediate risk from graduation.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1px;background:#000000;">
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2.5rem;">
